    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] text-center mb-12">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-[#39393A]/10 shadow-[0_1px_3px_rgba(57,57,58,0.08)]">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">What is a Hy-Tek HY3 file?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">HY3 is a file format created by Hy-Tek Sports Software. It's the standard way swimming clubs exchange entry and results data with meet promoters in the UK. If your county or regional meet uses Hy-Tek Meet Manager, they'll expect entries in this format.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-[#39393A]/10 shadow-[0_1px_3px_rgba(57,57,58,0.08)]">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">Do I need Hy-Tek Team Manager installed?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">No. Swimly generates and reads HY3 files natively. You don't need to buy or install any Hy-Tek software. Swimly replaces the need for Team Manager entirely for entry and results management.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-[#39393A]/10 shadow-[0_1px_3px_rgba(57,57,58,0.08)]">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">What about meets that use SportSystems?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">Swimly supports SportSystems CSV files as well. Between Hy-Tek and SportSystems, you're covered for roughly 90% of UK swimming competitions. The system auto-detects which format you're working with.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-[#39393A]/10 shadow-[0_1px_3px_rgba(57,57,58,0.08)]">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">How does PB tracking work?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">When you import results from a competition, Swimly automatically compares each time against the swimmer's existing personal best for that event and distance. If it's a new PB, it's flagged and recorded. Coaches and parents can see PB history in the swimmer's profile.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-[#39393A]/10 shadow-[0_1px_3px_rgba(57,57,58,0.08)]">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">Can I preview results before importing?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">Yes. Swimly has a preview mode that parses the file, validates the data, and shows you exactly what will be imported, including which swimmers were matched and any potential PBs, before anything is saved to your database.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface-raised border border-[#39393A]/10 shadow-[0_1px_3px_rgba(57,57,58,0.08)]">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-2">Does Swimly integrate with Swim England rankings?</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-soft">We're working towards Swim England API integration. In the meantime, you can import times and rankings from Swim England's Club Personnel Report (CSV export) or from competition result files. Your swimmers' SE numbers are stored and used for matching across all imports.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

